<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in Sept-Nov.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in Sept-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment fell to an average of 431,000 in the three months to November from 438,000 in the three months to October, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Sept-Nov 96    Aug-Oct 96   Sept-Nov 95</p>
<p> total number	   431,000	  438,000	  451,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.5		6.6		6.8</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Sept-Nov 96    Aug-Oct 96   Sept-Nov 95</p>
<p> total number	   432,000	  442,000	  452,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.5		6.7		6.8</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated as percentage of average 1995 labour force (6.596 million). By international standards, the CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 570 8500</p>
